Hi Karl,
Thanks for the useful code. Based on publications asking similar questions, MQM seems to be preferred.

My resulting plots from MQM have two very distinct peaks (LOD ~ 40 for both), but the valley does not drop below significance threshold. This is a fine mapping population, so there are plenty of recombinants in this region, but I'm not sure why the valley remains significant.
The peaks move around as well (see attached example of 4 iterations of the same code and data!) I do not understand why the peaks would move so much with mqmaugment - maybe the minprob is too low? I must be missing something, thank you for your assistance! Apologies that this discussion thread has circled back to my original question about plots moving around!

The two traits are thousand train weight (TGW) and grain width (GW), and the LOD scores mirror each other I believe because grain width impacts grain weight.

SynOpHIF <- convert2riself(SynOpHIF)
#  No. individuals:    129
#  Total markers:      33
#   No. markers:        2 31
#   Percent genotyped:  98.4
#   Genotypes (%):      AA:48.4  BB:51.6
#max missing markers per individual = 8, increase maxaugind from baseline
#lower minprob more augmented individuals are kept,  because MQM fills in missing markers with all likely genotypes
SynOpHIF_augment <- mqmaugment(SynOpHIF, maxaugind = 256, minprob = 0.1, verbose = TRUE)
autocofactors <- mqmautocofactors(SynOpHIF_augment, 10)
mqm_TGW <- mqmscan(SynOpHIF_augment, autocofactors, pheno.col = "TGW_BLUP")
mqm_GW <- mqmscan(SynOpHIF_augment, autocofactors, pheno.col = "GW_BLUP")

The cim() function, as discussed earlier has much finer resolution , and attaching the code and plot in case that is informative re- 2 peaks and valley.
SynOpHIF <- convert2riself(SynOpHIF)
#  No. individuals:    129
#  Total markers:      33
#   No. markers:        2 31
#   Percent genotyped:  98.4
#   Genotypes (%):      AA:48.4  BB:51.6
SynOpHIF <- fill.geno(SynOpHIF, method = "argmax")

SynOpData <- calc.genoprob(SynOpHIF, step = 0, map.function = "kosambi")

TGW_BLUP <- cim(SynOpData, pheno.col = "TGW_BLUP", method = "hk", window = 20)
GW_BLUP <- cim(SynOpData, pheno.col = "GW_BLUP", method = "hk", window = 20)
plot(GW_BLUP, TGW_BLUP)

